      "message": "I\u0027m not sure I follow; this code needs `remainder.len()` bytes of entropy so requests `SMCCC_TRNG_RND64(remainder.len() * u8::BITS)` bits of entropy, which are returned in registers x0-x2 (total 3*64 bits), when then copy those into the `entropy` array, which is used to give a programmatic way to sub-slice x0-x2 and only consumes `remainder.len()` bytes from it, so no entropy is wasted, right? Note that `entropy` might contain less than `MAX_BYTES_PER_CALL` bytes of entropy, btw!",
